I like this.  It works with the idea of raising other dead things like pets.

Here is another polymorph idea: have golem *bodies* be generated by polymorph
applied to enough stuff.  These golem bodies might then count as *one* item
of the appropriate type, thereby reducing the size of your pile if you just
leave the bodies in the pile and keep zapping.  (In my master list of 
polypile-defanging methods, this is essentially a variant of #1, the %-chance
to destroy an object.)   The golem bodies could be *animated* using a wand of 
turn undead.  A golem should be a pet if the golem body was blessed, neutral 
if uncursed, and the golem would attack if the body were cursed.

A possible correspondence might be:
	100 pounds of scrolls/books		Unanimated Straw Golem
	100 pounds of steel weapons/armor	Unanimated Iron Golem
	100 pounds of wood weapons/armor	Unanimated Wood Golem
	100 pounds of rocks or gems		Unanimated Stone Golem
	100 pounds of food/corpses/potions(?)	Unanimated Flesh Golem
Also, give a chance of generating a golem if there is less stuff than this,
perhaps eating up other stuff in the pile to make the required weight.

Or maybe make the correspondence
	 20 pounds of stuff == 1 Hit Die
This way, people who want a big pet can make it big, whereas people who don't
will be continually creating small golem bodies whether they like it or not.

Naturally, the range of golem types might have to be expanded to make this
work better.  I.e. create paper golems, water golems (for potions), 
crystal golems (potions(?), crystal balls, crystal plate mail) etc  so
that no type of objects is polymorph-safe.

